["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Dataset/ConfidentialityLevelType/red", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "For named recipients only. The dataset is highly confidential and shall be shared only with named recipients.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/Role", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property", "_:N951f113594994f74ae6c3332cfec0931", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/vulnerabilityExploitabilityAssessment", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A reference to a Vulnerability Exploitability eXchange (VEX) statement which provides information on whether a product is impacted by a specific vulnerability in an included package and, if affected, whether there are actions recommended to remediate. See also [NTIA VEX one-page summary](https://ntia.gov/files/ntia/publications/vex_one-page_summary.pdf).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SbomType/deployed", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "SBOM provides an inventory of software that is present on a system. This may be an assembly of other SBOMs that combines analysis of configuration options, and examination of execution behavior in a (potentially simulated) deployment environment.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/test", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Conducting controlled tests, experiments or simulations to verify that specific requirements regarding performance, functionality, robustness, etc. are met.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/ExpandedLicensing/WithAdditionOperator", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#nodeKind", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#IRI", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/SafetyIntegrityLevelType/dalD", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/SbomType/analyzed", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "SBOM generated through analysis of artifacts (e.g., executables, packages, containers, and virtual machine images) after its build. Such analysis generally requires a variety of heuristics. In some contexts, this may also be referred to as a \"3rd party\" SBOM.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Nb04e0266d3d647928291bebf64518101", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Security/statusNotes", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/postOfficeBoxNumber", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The number that identifies a PO box. A PO box is a box in a post office or other postal service location assigned to an organization where postal items may be kept.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:Naf7232d140884af9a127c3865f6d6d8f", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "_:N8fb41625c22a45d98f68df4b26c82531", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/ExpandedLicensing/ConjunctiveLicenseSet", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Portion of an AnyLicenseInfo representing a set of licensing information\nwhere all elements apply.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/issn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Serial Number (ISSN)](https://www.issn.org/understanding-the-issn/what-is-an-issn/) is an eight-digit identifier for serial publications and other continuing resources standardized by [ISO 3297](https://www.iso.org/standard/84536.html). It consists of two groups of four digits separated by a hyphen, where the final character is a check digit that may be an \"X\". The hyphen is retained when the identifier is stored electronically to maintain the standard 9-character string format (e.g., `1464-3693`). The ISSN is media-specific; the same journal title may be assigned different identifiers for its physical and digital versions.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N3abd13aaf37545ccaeeef4bf7a62b666", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/coordinatedBy", "globalId", "", ""]
